WEBVTT

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.370
You want to go back to training?

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.660
I thought you ran away.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:17.830
Kanata.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.620
I don't have anything against track and field.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:28.000
I just hate the fact that you're
pushing your lost dreams on me.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.290
I want to find and pursue my own dreams!

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.200
I'm going to space!

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.540
In order to do that, to protect my crew,
I'll need to be strong.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.790
Dad, you retired because of injuries.
If you trained me,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:42.290
you can push me hard
without getting me injured, right?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.410
Of course. I would never let you
hurt your precious body.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.160
It doesn't matter what your dreams are.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.620
As long as you maintain a perfect body,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.660
you will have an advantage
in whatever goal or target.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.750
So that's what that meant...

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.290
Dammit...

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.580
Hey, um...

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:16.120
Did you have to gather the whole crew?
It's just about the two of us, right?

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.620
Did the DNA results come out already?

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.790
You're going to announce the results now?

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:24.120
That's a life-changing big deal!

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.200
Stop making this more exciting than it is!

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.160
I'm getting super nervous now!

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.500
The results are, your DNAs...

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:35.370
...are a complete match.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.000
Huh?

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.000
What does that mean?

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.580
The DNA is the blueprint for the human body.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:46.000
It is nearly impossible for two people
to share the exact same DNA.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Therefore, the two of you are the same person.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.950
Huh?!

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.000
Are you an idiot? What does that even mean?!
Quit making stuff up!

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.620
These are all facts.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:03.500
Doesn't that mean the two of them
are identical twins?

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.750
Twins? Right, that would explain how...

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:11.080
No, twins can't be different ages.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:16.500
I considered the possibility that Funi was
in hibernation like Polina was,

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.870
but that doesn't fit with her own
memory of how she grew up.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.870
The other hypothesis is probably correct.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.660
What other hypothesis?

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.160
And it's not just Quitterie and Funi.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:35.450
That's the common element linking all of us
together in this murder scheme.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.750
We are all...

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.620
...clones.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.080
Clones...

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.080
How?!

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.370
You mean we're copies of people?!

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:48.410
Hold on a sec! All clones?!

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.870
You're totally making that up!

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.160
Think about it.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.660
The possibility that our "parents"
are actually our "originals"

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.250
that we were copied from.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.660
Our parents...

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.370
The originals...

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.410
Funi is... my clone?

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:11.450
Wait. Making a human clone is a felony.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.410
Why would anyone go through
the risks of doing such a thing?

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:17.080
I have a theory.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.830
My father is researching the technology
of transplanting memories.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:25.250
Doing that would allow a person
to essentially swap to a new body.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:28.750
By making a clone body, a person
could discard their aged body

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.700
and transfer to a younger, new clone body.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.870
But... But that's...

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.660
The goal is rejuvenation?!

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:41.160
My father planned to keep his research
to himself and rejuvenate his body.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:45.370
He also gathered together a group
of allies who wanted the same thing.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.000
The scientist who developed the technology...

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.250
The hospital director to create the clones,
head of the school to send the clones to,

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:58.870
the athlete, the singer, the artist, the noble.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:03.910
We're just vessels for our
originals' rejuvenation.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.200
"Somewhere in Mousanish
Day 88 of being lost in space"

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.540
"Somewhere in Mousanish
Day 88 of being lost in space"
Sorry I'm late.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:18.620
Well, well, quite impressive
isn't it, this VIP room?

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.450
It's been a while.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.870
Who is this?

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:26.410
Have you forgotten? We've met.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:30.370
I am Felice Genma, Luca's original.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.700
He's a famous artist, you know.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.540
I've never been interested in that stuff.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:39.450
So, seeing how you brought me here
instead of Mr. Esposito,

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.870
is it safe to assume we will be
discussing a nefarious plot?

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:44.580
Nefarious?

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.250
Like an evil organization.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.950
What are you laughing about?

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:52.330
You're the one that brought up this
whole clone rejuvenation nonsense.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.040
It almost got us arrested.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.290
Spare me. What was her name, Funicia?

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.080
We all agreed to one clone per person.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.910
You secretly made a backup
for some spare organs.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.700
Indeed.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:12.250
Thanks to that little stunt, I had to force
a 10 year old onto that team.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.790
I can't begin to describe how hard
I had to work to get that done.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.750
Easy now.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.830
What's wrong with that?!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.870
This plan wasn't happening without my hospital.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.790
I earned that privilege!

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:27.000
It was quite a roundabout plan--

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.000
using the camp as a way
to make them go missing.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.830
What other option did we have?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:35.160
We can't leave any corpses.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:38.040
The Genome Control Act...

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:41.950
Even a basic DNA check
would reveal that they are clones.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.370
What a stupid law.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:49.950
Rumor says finding illegal clones was
actually one of the goals of the law.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:55.660
You'd be surprised to hear some people
secretly make clones for their organs.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.790
Huh? What are you looking at me for?

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:02.410
In order to make sure no genetic information
of the clones could be found,

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:06.870
they needed to be "lost" in deep space
where they could never come back.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.000
That was the best move.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.750
I was quite surprised to learn
that such a thing existed.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:17.870
If it were to be revealed to the public,
it would cause quite a commotion.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:22.950
When was that thing even developed?

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:28.080
At any rate, this plan of ours is finished.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.830
I am never working with any of you again.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.580
Oh, how regretful.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:39.200
I really wanted to be reborn.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:45.750
You had some very peculiar requests,
making your clone have both sexes.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.950
And I'm grateful for that.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:56.250
It was my dream, becoming an ultimate being,
transcending the boundaries of sex.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:07:00.660
Luca was perfect. Oh, how regretful.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:04.500
I really wanted to be reborn.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.290
Artists are all so weird.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:12.120
But I did want to ask you all this:

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:19.160
I sent mine out to be adopted, but you all
raised your clones like children, yes?

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:24.950
Doesn't it bother you? Are your hearts
that strong, or are they immune to pain?

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:32.200
Good question. I let my servants raise mine
to make sure I wouldn't get emotional.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:35.370
I sent the second one out for adoption.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:41.870
The one for my vessel, though,
I needed to keep close to train her brain.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:48.330
For people like me and her, who have special
knowledge, this was necessary.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:52.660
Mr. Hoshijima, you also spent
some time training your clone.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:56.790
I was going to be a world-class athlete again.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:08:00.410
I was merely training my own body.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.750
Think of my clone as a son?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.080
Never.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:10.250
The Genome Control Act.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:15.040
The government can easily track down
the clones if they have the genetic data.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:18.160
So they're just going to kill us now,
because we're of no use!

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.950
You've got to be kidding me!

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:24.250
Not just kill. To prevent
our DNA from being found,

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:30.870
they threw us out to the distant,
dark, freezing loneliness of space.

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:38.500
I guess they gave my dad campaign funds
to adopt me and oppose the law.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.080
They were all in on it.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.660
Please, wait!

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:46.200
My mother is a compassionate person.
I can't believe any of this!

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.040
I can't say anything definite
about your situation, Aries.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:53.250
But if we assume everything
we've theorized so far is true...

00:08:53.250 --> 00:09:00.500
I hate to say this, but perhaps she isn't
your real mother and you just didn't know.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.000
But...

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:08.330
We don't know that. As long as we're stuck
out here, there's no way to know more.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:12.040
But it did strike me as odd
that so many members of our team

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.870
were adopted or raised by single parents.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:19.370
Some of us were kept at an arm's length
to prevent emotional attachment.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.370
Some were trained to inherit their specialties.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:24.540
The one thing in common is
that we weren't loved.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:29.660
But... But that's...

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.160
We...

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.000
We were vessels!

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.500
We...

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:39.870
I can't say I really liked Mom.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:44.120
But there is an assumption of love
between family members.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.160
I loved her,

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.120
and I wanted her to love me, too.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.000
Quitterie...

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.540
Let go of me!

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.450
We are family!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.370
No parents? Who cares!

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:13.160
Discarded clones? Who cares!

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:19.540
We were born under the same destiny
and overcame hardships together as a family!

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:23.580
Let's all go home together and surprise them.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:27.040
They don't know we're coming back.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:30.830
When we make it back, the originals
are all getting arrested

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.500
and we clones will all get new family registries.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.500
That's right! That will be our revenge!

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.450
We're not going to let them get away with this!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:47.370
Kanata told me once.
Survival tip number two:

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:52.250
Getting up will let you stand up.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.750
We're all getting home together.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:58.250
Then we'll become our own people!

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.950
"During faster-than-light travel
Day 89 of being lost in space"

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.620
What's wrong, you okay?

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.540
This title is way too long.

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:17.910
That's what's on your mind?

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:21.000
Oh, were you worried about me?

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.250
Sort of.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:24.200
I can't say I'm not shocked.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:28.120
But I've never met my original before.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.160
To be honest, it doesn't feel that real to me.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:32.450
Aren't you angry?

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:34.830
Of course I am. Tons of anger.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:38.870
But like you said,
we just need to get home safely.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:43.700
Then we can start a new life.
That's what my mind has settled on for now.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:49.040
I see. I was worried that everyone
might be depressed.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:52.700
You know how my sex is unclear, right?

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:56.120
It used to bother me a lot,
but it also taught me that

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.870
worrying about stuff that's
out of my control is a waste of time.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:02.000
I'd rather focus on how
to make things more fun.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:06.330
No matter what happens, the one who
enjoys the ride is always the winner.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:13.540
This trip, too. Nothing was as we expected,
but it's still pretty fun.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:17.450
I've grown to like how unique my body is.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:21.580
How I was born doesn't really matter.

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:24.250
Even if I'm a clone.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:26.000
I'm still me.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:32.000
We've got quite a decent surplus of food.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:37.080
We had quite a crisis on Icriss, but after that,
it was actually very smooth.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.700
You're a tough one, Charce.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:43.500
Aren't you bothered by what we found out?

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:46.330
Bothered? Of course.

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:52.700
But unlike the rest of you,
I already cut ties with my parents.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:55.870
Maybe that's what prevented me
from being hit too hard by this.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.910
Right, I see.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:00.660
How about you, though?

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:05.540
Your father trained you so much because he...

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:07.700
Sorry, never mind.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.500
No, it's okay.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:14.330
When I was lost in the mountains,
I saw my dad worried for the first time.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:19.250
Come to think of it, he was just
worried about his own body.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:25.080
When he trained me, he was just training
his new replacement body.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:30.080
But that doesn't change the fact
that I wanted the training.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.330
I chose it myself.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:36.750
I have to admit this body is proving
pretty useful, thanks to that.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.290
So, like, I don't mind.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:43.040
You're the tough one, Kanata.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:46.160
You have a strong mind, strong body,

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:49.950
strong bones, strong organs,
and nice fleshiness.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:53.290
You're sounding weirdly creepy!

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:56.040
Can you follow up with
the rest of the crew, Captain?

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.450
Aye, yeah.

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:02.410
Hey, take care of these too, please.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:03.500
Yeah.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.330
Need help?

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:11.660
Don't worry about me.
I'm not in shock or anything.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:16.160
In fact, I'm glad I figured out why
they treated me the way they did.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.290
Ulgar...

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.500
I'm not just trying to act tough.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.790
To be honest, I'm relieved.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:27.330
When I get back,
I'm going to go after Luca's dad.

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:30.700
I have to admit, I had hesitations about that.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:34.160
Now I don't have to feel bad at all
about throwing their butts in prison.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:37.790
You've lost your brother and you'll
be cutting ties with your mother...

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:39.410
You're going to be alone.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:43.370
You're out of character, boss.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:46.410
None of us are alone, right?

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:50.830
You're out of character, Ulgar-boy!

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:54.290
Stop it, stop wiggling!

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.830
Hey, how're you holding up?

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:01.660
I was crying for a while,
but I've calmed down now.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:06.580
Now I see why my mother
told me not to stand out.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:13.620
If I got attention on my own, it would be
inconvenient when she took over.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:16.290
I wonder what will happen when I get back.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:22.080
Like we said before, the originals will get
arrested and we start new lives.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:24.790
I see. That's...

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:28.910
That's really nice.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:32.660
It does hurt to lose my mother.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:36.080
But now I don't have to hold back anymore.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.500
I want to sing, a lot.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.830
I want to become a singer.

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:45.080
Can you start off at our party?

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.620
You got it.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.580
Clones... Who would've thought.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:58.790
There had to be something about you all,
but I never expected that...

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:02.910
We'll need the police
to figure out the details, but...

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:05.620
I feel we've gotten the overall story
pretty accurate.

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:08.000
Are you okay, Aries?

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:12.700
To be honest, I think I'm
the most confused about this.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:15.200
Even if we're right about everything,

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:20.540
there's still a lot of questions, like about
my mother and who I'm a clone of.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:25.120
But I do know that my mother's love is real.

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:27.750
So, I don't really care.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:34.580
Adults can lie,
but true emotions can't be faked.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:42.950
Even if I'm someone's clone,
my mother is still my mother.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.500
I believe in love.

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:57.200
Like this?

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.200
Yes. Open it up now.

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.040
Wow...

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:06.580
Quitterie, are you okay?

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:08.950
Yes, I am.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:12.330
I might not look it,
but I've mostly gotten over it.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.200
I've been living the life my mom
defined for me--until now.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.450
I used to think that was a good thing,

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:22.080
but I guess I was just doing that
to get her attention.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:27.080
Now that I know it's all a lie, I feel free...

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.450
Almost relieved, even.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:32.080
Okay. I'm glad.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:34.580
I've been worried, ya know?

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:41.870
Funicia, you're much tougher than I am,
even though we're the same person.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.200
I'm the idiot that won't stop crying.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:47.250
Genetics aren't the only thing
that determines personality.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:49.500
According to research in behavioral genetics,

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:53.290
the effects of genes and
the environment are about equal.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:56.540
Funi was raised in a different place
by different parents.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:59.580
She's no longer the same person as you.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:02.330
Genetics don't matter.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:07.950
I am who I am because of
who I'm with and what I experience.

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:10.700
This trip changed me.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:13.700
I'm so happy that it did.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.160
Quitterie.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.080
What?

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:23.790
It is what it is.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:27.040
You know, with all the things that happened,
it was getting kind of gloomy.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:31.910
I figured now would be
a good time to discuss this...

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:33.750
You're getting married?!

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:39.290
Wait, what? You're getting married? Huh?

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:41.250
How did this happen?

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:44.870
Let me introduce to you my fiancée,
Quitterie Rafaeli.

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.160
He's playing us, I know for sure!

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:48.950
Are you serious?

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:50.040
I am.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:53.120
--Good job, Zack!
--Ow!

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:56.870
So that's what you were
discussing this whole time?

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.450
So lucky! So lucky...

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:04.620
I knew it. Zack is secretly a great womanizer,
and the disinterest in girls was a front!

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.580
Congratulations, Quitterie!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:07.620
Thank you.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:10.450
So lucky! So lucky! So lucky!

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:13.500
Hey, who confessed to who first?!

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:18.160
It doesn't matter who said it first.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:22.330
This marriage was predetermined
from a long time ago.

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.290
Whoa, whoa, what, what?

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:26.870
What's the deal with this guy? He's dangerous!

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:33.870
Wait, to be clear, you guys
were dating this whole time?

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:36.290
Quitterie's feelings were obvious to all of us,

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:39.700
but did Zack have feelings for her too?
That's what you need to clear up for us!

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.580
Wait, slow down, what are you all saying?!

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:46.500
Of course I did.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.120
"Of course"!

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.660
Hey, something exploded just now!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:52.790
Oh, wow, Zack! Oh, wow!

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:57.500
No! I can't stay here.
This is doing weird stuff to my heart!

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:00.160
It's impossible to read his emotions.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:02.160
I can't read them either!

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:04.410
No, you've got it all wrong!

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:06.450
Zack is trying to hide it,

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:10.580
but you've gotten closer
to each other during this trip, right?

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:12.540
No, Aries! Stand back!

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:18.250
I've always been at her side,
and that will never change.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.540
Stop Aries! This guy is trouble!

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:23.330
He's got the big guns
and he's not afraid to use them!

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:27.040
So what is it about Quitterie
that you like so much?

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.040
Stop pushing on so bravely!

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.200
Huh? Isn't it obvious how cute she is?

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:35.500
Stop it! I can't handle it anymore!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.830
Luca, sorry, we're going to need
to change the name of the party again.

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:39.830
Seriously?

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:41.080
Yeah.

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:47.500
"'Farewell to Icriss & Welcome aboard Sis Lina!
& Best Wishes Zack and Quitterie!"

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:48.950
Focus!

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.410
Team B5 camp log.

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:58.040
No matter what happens,
this team is positive, strong,

00:20:58.040 --> 00:20:59.580
and invincible.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.040
What is this, a warning?

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:09.040
No, we finally got the image.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:13.950
I fixed the broken space telescope
using parts I found on the <i>Ark VI</i>.

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:16.540
We can see planets 2,000 light years away.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.200
In other words...

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:20.250
...home sweet home.

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:23.200
Seriously?!

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:25.200
Whoa, I'm getting goose bumps!

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:27.580
Really? We can see it?

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:32.080
Yes... Blue ocean, white clouds, green lands.

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:37.290
It feels so far in the past.
We've been gone for like three months now.

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:40.950
Just one more planet before we get home.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:43.370
Hey, Yunhua's crying!

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:45.870
You too, Funi.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:48.750
Nothing weird about that.

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:51.330
It's only natural to cry seeing this.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.910
Okay, let's get going.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.700
To the final planet!

00:21:56.700 --> 00:21:58.950
Aye, yeah!

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:03.040
Why is everyone so excited?

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:04.250
Polina.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:06.620
The telescope is up and running!

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:09.160
We got a glimpse of the goal--
everyone's hyped up.

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:13.410
Oh, I see Earth...!

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:18.540
This isn't a dream, I am going home...

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:20.870
Polina...

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:23.330
I've dreamed of this so many times.

00:22:23.330 --> 00:22:26.700
The oceans, the continents...

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:30.870
Hmm? Something is wrong.

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:32.910
Is this really Earth?

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:39.160
I mean, is that Africa?
No, the shape is all wrong.

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:41.540
What is that island over there?

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:43.950
What's wrong, Polina?

00:22:43.950 --> 00:22:47.500
No, this isn't Earth...

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:52.160
You've got the wrong planet,
check your results again!

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:54.370
Hey, Polina...

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:56.450
What's "Earth"?

00:22:58.200 --> 00:23:02.790
What? Is this a prank? Earth is Earth!

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:04.500
Why are you looking at me like that?!

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:07.950
Earth! Our home planet!

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:10.370
Wait... What's going on?

00:23:10.370 --> 00:23:12.500
You're being weird, Polina.

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:15.500
Is her memory still unclear?

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:18.160
Are you okay, Polina?

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:21.290
Is it me? Am I crazy?

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:25.580
Please, tell me you're joking... Or...

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:28.540
What is that planet?!

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:31.450
If that's not Earth,

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:34.160
where did you all come from?!

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:37.660
Our planet?

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:40.200
That's obvious.

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:44.790
Planet...

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:47.580
...Astra.
